Every limit of Proposition <a href="#geo:compactness" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="geo:compactness">11</a> inherits the conditional crossing estimates needed below in its natural driving filtration. They hold after a live stopping time and after localization on a finite interval on which the relevant Loewner coordinates remain nondegenerate. In the following two estimates, reset capacity time to zero at the chosen live stopping time.*

1.  *In the current half-plane chart, put the tip at $0$, rescale a given live point to modulus $1$, and write $x$ for its real part. If its imaginary part is small, so $x$ is near $1$ or $-1$, then $$\mathbb P\{\text{the future trace visits }B(x,d)\mid\text{past}\}
     \le Kd^\alpha$$ for all sufficiently small $d$.*

2.  *For a live physical point $w$, $$\mathbb P\left\{
       \inf_{s\text{ before swallowing}}
       \operatorname{crad}_{O_s}(w)
          <\varepsilon\,\operatorname{crad}_{O_0}(w)
       \,\middle|\,\text{past at the restart}\right\}
     \le K\varepsilon^\alpha .$$*

*The assertions apply in particular at inverse elapsed-clock times and at first angular-level crossings used in Section <a href="#eng:section" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="eng:section">4</a>. No semimartingale property of the driver is assumed here.

For $$\label{eng:J-definition}
 J_t=\int_{\mathbb H}\frac{\mu_t(v)}{|v|^2}\,\mathrm dA(v),$$ there is a constant $K<\infty$ such that $$\label{eng:energy-bound}
 \mathbb E\int_0^\infty J_t^2\,\mathrm dt
 \le K m^2\operatorname{area}(\Omega)<\infty.$$ Consequently $J_t$ is finite for almost every capacity time, almost surely.

There are $a>0$, $K<\infty$, and $d_*>0$ with the following properties. They hold conditionally on the past at every stopping time $\tau$ on the event $w\in O_\tau$.*

1.  *Translate and dilate the current half-plane chart so that its tip is $0$, its target is $\infty$, and $|Z_\tau|=1$. If $X_\tau\le d_*$ and $x=\operatorname{Re}(Z_\tau/|Z_\tau|)$, then, for $0<d<d_*$, the probability that the restarted trace visits $B(x,d)$ is at most $Kd^a$.*


2.  *With $R=\operatorname{crad}_{O_\tau}(w)$ and $0<\varepsilon<1$, $$\label{eng:bulk-crad}
     \mathbb P\left\{
       \inf_{\tau\le t<T_w}\operatorname{crad}_{O_t}(w)<\varepsilon R
          \,\middle|\,\mathcal F_\tau\right\}
     \le K\varepsilon^a.$$ The infimum in this formula is strictly before the lifetime. Conformal radius is not assigned the value zero upon swallowing.*

*These estimates remain valid for the inverse-clock stopping times and the first angular-level stopping times used below.

Consider a chordal Loewner trace in $\mathbb H$ with continuous driver, starting from $0$. Let its maps be $l_t$, so that $l_0$ is the identity. Start a point at $z_0=x+\mathrm iX_0$ with $|z_0|=1$. There are absolute constants $c_0>0$ and $K<\infty$ such that, if $0<d<1/8$, $X_0\le c_0d$, and the trace avoids $B(x,d)$, then up to the point’s lifetime $$\label{eng:avoidance-deterministic}
 \sup_s\frac{X_s}{X_0}\le\frac Kd,
 \qquad
 \int_0^{\sigma_*}\frac{X_s}{X_0}\,\mathrm ds\le\frac Kd.$$ Consequently $$\label{eng:avoidance-square}
 \int_0^{\sigma_*}\left(\frac{X_s}{X_0}\right)^2\mathrm ds
 \le\frac K{d^2}.$$

At every live restart, use elapsed point clock and write $X_0$ for its starting angular coordinate. There are $a>0$ and $K<\infty$ such that $$\label{eng:supremum-tail}
 \mathbb P\left\{\sup_{s\ge0}\frac{X_s}{X_0}>u
       \,\middle|\,\text{past}\right\}\le Ku^{-a},\qquad u\ge1.$$ Moreover the conditional laws of $$\label{eng:occupation}
 I=\int_0^\infty\left(\frac{X_s}{X_0}\right)^2\mathrm ds$$ are uniformly tight, over all live restarts and all starting angles.

For the $p$ in Lemma <a href="#eng:decay" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="eng:decay">21</a>, there are $\epsilon>0$ and $K<\infty$ such that, uniformly over every initial live point, $$\label{eng:weighted-clock}
 \mathbb E\int_0^{\sigma_*}X_s^{2p}
 \left[
   \left(\frac{\sqrt{t(s)}}{r_s}\right)^\epsilon
  +\left(\frac{r_s}{\sqrt{t(s)}}\right)^\epsilon
 \right]\mathrm ds\le K.$$ Here $t(s)$ is capacity elapsed from the chosen starting instant. The value at $s=0$ is immaterial.

Let $\kappa>0$, and let $b(t,x)$ be a fixed progressively measurable nonanticipating real functional on continuous paths starting at zero. There is at most one law of a continuous weak solution of $$\label{uni:generic-SDE}
 \mathrm dX_t=\sqrt\kappa\,\mathrm dB_t+b(t,X)\mathrm dt,
 \qquad X_0=0,$$ among solutions satisfying $$\label{uni:generic-energy}
 \int_0^T b(t,X)^2\mathrm dt<\infty\quad\hbox{almost surely}$$ for every finite $T$.

With the first $J$ levels and their finite set $H$ fixed, let all $H$-cut preimages have diameter at most $\rho$. Uniformly conditional on the two explored heads, the probability that the shielding procedure fails is bounded by $$\begin{aligned}
 &K|H|\rho^\alpha\\
 &\quad+K\sum_{k>J}2^k
     \prod_{j_*\le j<k}K\bigl(2^{-j}(j+2)^2\bigr)^\alpha\\
 &\quad+K\delta_n^{-2}
     \prod_{j_*\le j\le N_n}K\bigl(2^{-j}(j+2)^2\bigr)^\alpha
 +o(1).
 \end{aligned}
 \label{loc:failure-bound}$$ Here $j_*$ and the constants are independent of $J,n$ and of the unbounded part of the domain. In particular, the failure probability tends to zero by first taking $J$ large, then $\rho$ small at that stage, and finally the mesh sufficiently small.
